10. Error and fallback behavior

OAuth unavailable, recent status line exists

Return status-line snapshot.
Show a non-blocking OAuth warning in provider settings.
Do not invoke /usage.

OAuth unavailable, status line stale, manual refresh

Offer or run authorized /usage.
If declined, show cached data.

OAuth unavailable during background refresh

Use recent status line.
Otherwise use cache.
Never open Claude CLI.

/usage fails but status-line snapshot appeared during probe

Read the newly written status-line snapshot.
Use it if valid and newer than the prior snapshot.

Account changed

Do not show the old account’s result as current.
Quarantine incompatible snapshots and cache entries.
Prompt the user to refresh.

Network lost

Do not run /usage merely because OAuth has a network error.
Show recent passive or cached data.
Retry after network recovery.

