11. Security requirements

* Keep OAuth tokens in Keychain or Claude-owned credential storage.
* Never copy tokens into the app’s usage cache.
* Never log authorization headers.
* Redact token-like values from all error descriptions.
* Use fixed executable paths and fixed CLI arguments.
* Do not launch the Claude probe through a shell.
* Disable tools in probe sessions.
* Use an isolated non-project working directory.
* Keep bridge and cache files private to the current user.
* Validate ownership and permissions before reading credential files.
* Reject symlink-based credential and snapshot paths where appropriate.
* Use atomic writes.
* Bound subprocess execution time and output.
* Clear sensitive in-memory buffers where practical.
* Never upload Claude usage or identity data.

