14. Completion criteria

The Claude provider is complete when:

* OAuth provides fresh five-hour and weekly usage on a valid Claude Code account.
* OAuth failures fall back to a recent status-line snapshot.
* /usage never runs automatically in the background.
* A user can authorize and run /usage from a manual refresh.
* A failed live refresh preserves and clearly labels cached data.
* Every displayed result identifies its source and capture time.
* Stale and expired windows are not presented as live.
* Account changes do not leak or merge prior account data.
* No credential appears in logs, cache files, diagnostics, test fixtures, or crash output.
* The implementation passes source-specific and coordinator fallback tests.
* Real-account verification shows acceptable parity between OAuth and Claude’s own /usage display.

